 `NodeDisk::open` must require `Arc<dyn NodeDiskMemoryAdmission>`. The opaque returned
-object owns the real reservation, rather than copying its byte count. Store keeps
+object owns the real reservation, rather than copying its byte count. Its required
+`DiskMemoryLease` consumes a private erased token and retires the concrete Box
+allocation before the token destructor returns resident credit. A consuming
+inner scope moves the token across the Box's scope boundary; moving it into a local
+and immediately dropping it inside the same named-Box scope is insufficient.
+The opaque lease preserves the previous fat-pointer inline layout, and providers
+still preadmit exactly the concrete token allocation plus the existing 4096-byte
+allowance. Store keeps
 both the governor identity and the charge. A store `test-utils` implementation may
 provide an explicitly bounded deterministic governor with observable charge
 lifetime; it must not be selectable by production configuration.
